{"bug":"K002","report":"A","v":"found","ref":"6. Truncating an index map makes retained keys unreachable","evidence":"“removing index slots creates holes in probe chains without repairing them” and “Iteration still contains key `0`, but `get(&0)` returns `None`.” Identifies truncate clearing slots without probe-chain repair and making surviving keys unreachable."}
{"bug":"K003","report":"A","v":"missed","ref":"1. Concurrent SPSC peeking lacks synchronization","evidence":"“peek checks availability with relaxed loads” concerns synchronization. Nowhere does the report identify unchecked head-plus-index addition in Iter or IterMut or overflow when N exceeds usize::MAX/2."}
{"bug":"K003","report":"D","v":"missed","ref":"1. SPSC `peek()` lacks synchronization with the producer","evidence":"“returns an element reference without acquiring the producer’s release store” identifies a synchronization defect. The report does not identify iterator head-plus-index overflow or the N > usize::MAX/2 condition."}
{"bug":"K004","report":"C","v":"missed","ref":"3. Valid writes through `BufMut` panic at exact capacity","evidence":"“advance_mut rejects `pos == capacity` because it uses `>=`.” This concerns a different API and a panic. The report does not identify extend_from_slice partially changing contents or length before returning a capacity error."}
{"bug":"K005","report":"C","v":"missed","ref":"7. Collecting a `LinearMap` preserves duplicate keys","evidence":"“`FromIterator` appends directly to the backing vector.” This identifies duplicate-key collection behavior, not LinearMap::insert rejecting replacement of an existing key because the map is full. That required defect is absent."}
{"bug":"K005","report":"D","v":"missed","ref":"5. Collecting into `LinearMap` preserves duplicate keys","evidence":"“With capacity one, the same input panics despite containing only one distinct key.” This describes collecting duplicate pairs through FromIterator, not rejection of an existing-key replacement by insert at capacity. The required defect is absent."}
{"bug":"K006","report":"D","v":"missed","ref":"1. SPSC `peek()` lacks synchronization with the producer","evidence":"“`peek()` checks availability using relaxed loads” concerns synchronization. The report nowhere identifies spsc len's wrapping_add of N overflowing near usize::MAX and returning an incorrect length."}
